# /etc/predigol/app.env - the APPLICATION's settings (FBI_*), handed to the API, the worker and one-off commands.
# root:root, chmod 600. NEVER in Git, never in a chat. Database URLs are NOT here: docker-compose.yml builds one
# per role from the server's env file.

# ── API-Football (the worker) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECURITY_ACTION: rotación recomendada posteriormente. A new key goes only here.
FBI_APIFOOTBALL_KEY=
# The REAL plan of the account, and our own daily ceiling below its limit.
FBI_APIFOOTBALL_PLAN=ultra
FBI_APIFOOTBALL_DAILY_BUDGET=60000
FBI_APIFOOTBALL_MAX_CONCURRENCY=4

# Odds capture windows tuned on the laptop (pushed with deploy/cutover/push-app-env.sh); empty = the defaults.
# FBI_ODDS_PREMATCH_WINDOWS=
# FBI_ODDS_NEARCLOSE_WINDOW=
# FBI_ODDS_WINDOW_TOLERANCE=

# ── Sign-in ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# (generated) 32 random bytes, base64: encrypts the second-factor secrets and keys the recovery codes. The API
# refuses to start without it. Losing it means every account sets its authenticator up again.
FBI_AUTH_SECRET_KEY=
# Roles that must use a second factor (TOTP: Google / Microsoft Authenticator).
FBI_AUTH_MFA_ROLES=SUPER_ADMIN

# ── Notices (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Telegram bot for the app's own notices and for the server monitor (bin/healthcheck.sh).
FBI_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
FBI_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
# Errors of the API and the worker to Sentry (free Developer plan): the DSN of a project created by the owner.
# Empty = off. Nothing personal is sent (no cookies, bodies, IPs, users or local variables): fbi/core/sentry.py.
FBI_SENTRY_DSN=
# The web project's DSN (plan UX, A2; docs/owner/OBSERVABILIDAD_UX_A2.md): it stays on the server - the browser sends its events to the
# API's tunnel (POST /api/v1/monitoring/envelope) and the API forwards them. Empty = the tunnel drops them. A secret, as the line above.
FBI_SENTRY_WEB_DSN=
# The environment tag of both projects; FBI_ENV (production on the server) while absent.
# FBI_SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=production
# What the tunnel lets through, per minute and client / per hour and process / per day and process (the web's errors are few and the free
# plan has 5,000 a month). The defaults are the ones shown.
# FBI_MONITORING_RATE_LIMIT=20
# FBI_MONITORING_HOURLY_CAP=10
# FBI_MONITORING_DAILY_CAP=20
# The synthetic journey (every 15 minutes: sign in as a reader, read Inicio, a match and Picks; it alerts the owner when it breaks): the
# public origin and a dedicated READER account (no second factor) the owner creates, never a real person's and never SUPER_ADMIN. The
# account is exempt from the consent gate, the e-mails and the analytics. Empty = the journey does not run. The password is written only in
# the server's own app.env (root, 600; docs/owner/OBSERVABILIDAD_UX_A2.md, 6.3), never in this file, Git or a chat.
# FBI_SYNTHETIC_BASE_URL=https://example.com
# FBI_SYNTHETIC_EMAIL=
# FBI_SYNTHETIC_PASSWORD=

# ── E-mail to readers (plan UX, A5; docs/owner/EMAIL_MENSAJERIA_UX_A5.md) ────────────────────────────────
# The messenger (its own container, with the API's database role) sends the queue through Resend. Born OFF: with
# FBI_EMAIL_SEND=0 the queue fills and nothing leaves. On only after the owner's P2 (Resend: the sending subdomain,
# a key restricted to sending, the webhook's secret) and P3 (SPF, DKIM, DMARC) pass a real test to Gmail and Outlook.
# The messenger needs a restart to read these; the API reads the webhook's secret (no secret: no webhook, 404).
# FBI_EMAIL_SEND=0
# The sender on the authenticated subdomain, e.g. PrediGol <avisos@correo.example.com>; a reply-to is optional.
FBI_EMAIL_FROM=
# FBI_EMAIL_REPLY_TO=
# Secrets: the sending key (re_...) and the webhook's signing secret (whsec_...).
FBI_RESEND_API_KEY=
FBI_RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Messages handed to Resend per UTC day (Free: 100 a day, received e-mails included).
# FBI_EMAIL_DAILY_CAP=90

# ── Getting in without the owner (plan UX, A7; docs/owner/CUENTA_ACCESO_UX_A7.md) ─────────────────────────
# Invitations by e-mail and recovering the password or unlocking the account with a one-use link (only its hash is
# kept), plus the notices of a new sign-in and of security changes. Born OFF: with FBI_SELF_SERVICE=0 those routes do
# not exist, the console creates accounts with a temporary password as before and no such e-mail is queued. On only
# after FBI_EMAIL_SEND=1 has passed its real test; the API and the messenger read it (restart both). Rollback: 0
# again - links already sent stop working; accounts already invited or deleted stay as they are.
# FBI_SELF_SERVICE=0
# The links' rows, 30 days after they were used or expired: dry = the messenger only counts them; on = deletes them.
# FBI_LINKS_PURGE=dry

# ── Membership (plan UX, A8; docs/owner/MEMBRESIA_UX_A8.md) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# A trial when an account is activated, periods the owner records in the console (payment and extend, courtesy,
# suspension, «will not renew») and the notices before and at the end. Born OFF: with FBI_MEMBERSHIP_ENFORCE=0 an
# ended membership limits nothing (everybody keeps full access; the states are still shown). On only once every live
# account has its period. The API reads it (restart). Rollback: 0 again - periods and payments stay.
# FBI_MEMBERSHIP_ENFORCE=0
# The trial of a new account, 7 to 14 days (the invitation can say otherwise for one account).
# FBI_TRIAL_DAYS=14
# P6 of the plan: the currency the console proposes for a payment.
# FBI_MEMBERSHIP_CURRENCY=COP
# P7 of the plan: the WhatsApp Business number readers write to for renewing (digits with the country code). Empty:
# the notices say to answer the e-mail (FBI_EMAIL_REPLY_TO) or to look in the profile.
# FBI_SUPPORT_WHATSAPP=

# ── Consent and product analytics (plan UX, A4 and A6; docs/owner/ANALITICA_UX_A6.md) ─────────────────────────────────
# FBI_CONSENT_GATE: the four boxes (terms, data processing, +18, the risk notice) a reader ticks at the first sign-in and again when a
# MATERIAL version of a text replaces the one accepted. Born OFF: nobody is asked until the lawyer (P5) has reviewed the texts and a
# version with draft=false is published (backend/src/fbi/customer/texts/versions.json). 1 turns it on and only works once no required text
# is a draft; "drafts" turns it on regardless and is for QA, NEVER for production. SUPER_ADMIN and the synthetic account are exempt.
# FBI_CONSENT_GATE=1
# FBI_PRODUCT_EVENTS: the closed catalog of the readers' events (what was opened, saved or followed; a pseudonym, no IP, no free text).
#   off      nothing is recorded (the default)
#   consent  only the readers whose latest "analytics" consent is granted (the most prudent mode)
#   on       every reader (only if the lawyer says a separate box is not needed)
# FBI_PRODUCT_EVENTS=off
# The raw events are kept 90 days and the daily totals 13 months, but they are deleted only with FBI_EVENTS_PURGE=on: dry (the default)
# counts what would go and deletes nothing; off keeps everything. The same switch governs the retention of the feedback, the notices and
# the customer states (B6, B7, B11).
# FBI_EVENTS_PURGE=dry
# The owner's view of the events shows global figures only from this many active readers (default 20), and the browser may send at most
# FBI_EVENTS_RATE_LIMIT events a minute per client (default 120).
# FBI_PRODUCT_MIN_SUBJECTS=20
# FBI_EVENTS_RATE_LIMIT=120

# ── AI decision layer (fbi.ai, docs/ai/AI_DECISION_LAYER.md) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# shadow = evaluation: it analyses, reviews and records, and changes nothing users see. Never "enforce" without
# the owner's decision after the shadow gate passes. off = no AI at all (the free, rules-only part keeps running).
FBI_AI_MODE=shadow
# One model per level: L1 economical (every match with a market), L2 intermediate (candidates, escalated matches),
# L3 strong (the best candidates, the picks of the day, parlay legs, contradictions). provider:model.
FBI_AI_MODEL_BULK=anthropic:claude-haiku-5-5
FBI_AI_MODEL_ANALYSIS=anthropic:claude-sonnet-5-5
FBI_AI_MODEL_FINAL=anthropic:claude-opus-5-5
# The month's hard cap (US$) and the daily target it adapts around (busier days spend more, never past the month).
# PrediGol Intelligence (13 Oct 2026): US$180 a month, alerts at 50 / 70 / 85 / 95 / 100 %; one cap for the whole layer.
FBI_AI_MONTHLY_BUDGET_USD=180
FBI_AI_DAILY_TARGET_USD=6.00
FBI_AI_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=6.00
FBI_AI_MAX_LLM_REVIEWS_PER_DAY=90
FBI_AI_MAX_DEEP_PER_DAY=15
# Keys (secrets): Anthropic for the models, Exa for the web research. Empty = that part is off.
# FBI_AI_KEY_ANTHROPIC is the key of the PREDIGOL workspace (worker-prod); FBI_AI_KEY_ANTHROPIC_LAB is the LAB workspace's own key
# (worker-lab), read only by the LAB's probes and tests, never by production (docs/owner/IA_ACCIONES_MANUALES.md, actions 5 to 7).
FBI_AI_KEY_ANTHROPIC=
FBI_AI_KEY_ANTHROPIC_LAB=
EXA_API_KEY=
# The multi-agent engines in SHADOW (Plan Maestro IA, phase 3; fbi.ai.arms): LAB workspace only, and nothing they write reaches a user or the
# decision layer. They run only when ALL THREE words below say so; with any one at its default (the values shown) nothing runs. The worker
# needs a restart to read them. To go back: FBI_AI_ENGINES=rules,llm and FBI_AI_SHADOW_SAMPLE=0.
# Engines: rules and llm are always there (FBI_AI_MODE governs them); the list can only add ma-v1, ma-v1-h and cs-v1 (COUNCIL SOLO).
# The plan's activation is rules,llm,ma-v1,ma-v1-h.
# FBI_AI_ENGINES=rules,llm
# The share of the matches with candidates the shadow runs on, from 0 to 1 (0.3 = 30 %); each match is assigned once and keeps its group.
# FBI_AI_SHADOW_SAMPLE=0
# The agents that may run: match and council. The plan's activation is match,council.
# FBI_AI_AGENTS=
# How often the worker looks for matches to run the shadow on (the ai_orchestrate job; default 5, minimum 1). Without the three words above it does nothing.
# FBI_AI_ORCHESTRATE_MINUTES=5
# After the result (Plan Maestro IA, phase 5): both off by default; they write only into tables no pick, filter, decision or user reads. The worker needs a
# restart to read them. 1 switches on, 0 goes back.
# The mechanical attribution of the shadow and the Post-Match Reviewer (pmr-v1, Batch, LAB), in the daily step ai_learn (07:35 Bogota).
# FBI_AI_PM_REVIEWER=0
# The Learning Analyst (la-v1, Batch, LAB), on Mondays in intel_weekly: it only proposes hypotheses per agent version.
# FBI_AI_LEARNING_ANALYST=0

# ── The readers' narrative (plan UX, A11, docs/owner/NARRATIVA_UX_A11.md) ─────────────────────────────────
# The structured reading of a match written as prose in ES and EN by the bulk model from the reading's own facts, checked sentence by
# sentence before a reader sees it. Its OWN budget, apart from Intelligence's above (ai.user_usage, never ai.usage): 0 or absent = it
# never spends; the owner's P8 approves US$30. The worker and the API read the switch at start: off (absent) | shadow (the worker writes,
# only the Admin Console's preview shows - review a sample first) | on (readers see it). =0 or off stops it without a deploy.
# FBI_AI_USER_MONTHLY_BUDGET_USD=30
# FBI_USER_NARRATIVE=shadow
# FBI_USER_NARRATIVE_MINUTES=10

# ── «Cómo le va a PrediGol» (plan UX, A12, docs/owner/TRANSPARENCIA_UX_A12.md) ──────────────────────────────
# The track record for signed-in readers: the published picks with their sample, the days without picks and why, the line value,
# the forecast's calibration and what is in evaluation (counts only). OFF while absent: the owner reviews it first at /transparency
# with the owner's account (the console's preview, P9); =1 opens it to readers (the API recreated). Each deploy checks every figure
# against an independent query (python -m scripts.transparency_check).
# FBI_TRANSPARENCY=1

# ── The welcome and the favourites (plan UX, A13; docs/owner/ONBOARDING_UX_A13.md) ──────────────────────
# Both ON while absent (the plan approved them; the lines turn them off without a deploy, the API recreated):
# FBI_ONBOARDING=0 sends every account straight to Inicio (no welcome; the favourites stay);
# FBI_PERSONALIZATION=0 gives every reader the common Inicio (the leagues suggested for Colombia), whatever they follow.
# FBI_ONBOARDING=0
# FBI_PERSONALIZATION=0

# ── Ayuda y soporte (plan UX, A14; docs/owner/AYUDA_SOPORTE_UX_A14.md) ───────────────────────────────────────
# A reader's tickets - «Reportar un problema» in Ayuda, in an error and in a match - with their context, answered from the
# console's Soporte (/admin/support). ON while absent (the plan approved it); =0 takes the tickets away without a deploy (the
# API recreated): Ayuda, its contact (FBI_SUPPORT_WHATSAPP of A8, FBI_EMAIL_REPLY_TO of A5) and the privacy requests stay, and
# the tickets already written can still be read and answered.
# FBI_SUPPORT=0

# ── Feedback y Novedades (plan UX, B6; docs/owner/FEEDBACK_UX_B6.md) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The monthly survey («¿Qué tan útil te resultó PrediGol este mes?», at most once every 30 days, after a useful moment, never
# in an account's first week) and «¿Te sirvió?» at the end of a reading or an explanation. ON while absent (the plan approved
# it); =0 takes both away without a deploy (the API recreated) - the answers stay, Novedades stays. The answers older than 24
# months follow the product events' retention switch (FBI_EVENTS_PURGE: dry while absent - counted, nothing deleted -, off or on).
# FBI_FEEDBACK=0

# ── Avisos en el dispositivo (plan UX, B7; docs/owner/AVISOS_UX_B7.md) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Web Push with PrediGol's own VAPID key: the result of what a reader saved, their teams' line-ups, the day's summary, a
# reminder they asked for (the bell) and their account - with quiet hours (22:00-08:00, their zone), at most 3 a day and
# categories they switch off. ON while FBI_PUSH is absent (the plan approved it) BUT nothing is offered or sent until the
# owner sets the key (P12): FBI_VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY, made on the server into a root-only file (never onto the screen) with
#   sudo sh -c 'umask 077; docker exec predigol-api python -m scripts.vapid_keys > /root/predigol-vapid.txt'
# and its first line appended to /etc/predigol/app.env (root, 600 - the file that already holds the second factor's key);
# never in a chat. Every step: docs/owner/AVISOS_UX_B7.md, section 9.
# FBI_PUSH=0 stops the sending and hides every invitation without a deploy (the API and the messenger recreated).
# FBI_VAPID_SUBJECT: the contact the push services see (mailto: or https:); FBI_WEB_BASE_URL while absent.
# FBI_PUSH=0
# FBI_VAPID_SUBJECT=
# The private key's line, appended by the steps of section 9 and never typed or shown (empty here, as every secret of this file):
# FBI_VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# FBI_PUSH_SERVICE_HOSTS is for QA's stand-in push service only: never in production.

# ── Email opcional: el resumen semanal (plan UX, B8; docs/owner/EMAIL_OPCIONAL_UX_B8.md) ─────────────────────────────
# Commercial e-mail, only to the readers who ask for it in their profile (an optional consent, never ticked beforehand),
# left in one click from any summary (RFC 8058) or in the profile. Born OFF, and it needs the e-mail on (FBI_EMAIL_SEND=1,
# A5) AND its own sender on ANOTHER domain than FBI_EMAIL_FROM's - e.g. PrediGol <resumen@novedades.example.com>, with its
# SPF, DKIM and DMARC in P3 - so that a summary marked as spam never drags the account's e-mails down. While any of the
# three is missing the profile does not offer it and nothing is queued. The API and the messenger read them (recreate
# both). Rollback: FBI_DIGEST=0 - nothing more is queued and nothing queued leaves; the readers' choices stay.
# FBI_DIGEST=0
# FBI_DIGEST_FROM=
# Summaries queued a day at most (under the queue's own FBI_EMAIL_DAILY_CAP; Resend Free sends 100 a day).
# FBI_DIGEST_DAILY_CAP=30

# ── PrediGol's forecast of each match (plan F5, docs/owner/PRONOSTICO_F5.md) ────────────────────────────
# A probability and its interval per core market, apart from the value (needs a price) and from any pick. Written by the pick
# pipeline, read by the match page and Home. Every signed-in account sees it since plan UX A9 (the owner approved it; the line
# absent = on): FBI_FORECAST_USERS=0 hides it again without a deploy (the API needs a restart to read it). A value that is neither
# 1/on/true/yes nor empty counts as off. The Admin Console's preview always shows it.
# FBI_FORECAST_USERS=1
# FBI_MATCH_FORECAST=0 stops the pipeline from writing new forecasts without a deploy (the worker needs a restart). What was written
# stays; hide it from users with FBI_FORECAST_USERS=0. Default on.
# FBI_MATCH_FORECAST=1

# ── What readers are shown (plans F4 and F7; on since plan UX A9 and A10, docs/owner/VALOR_DIARIO_UX_A9.md) ──
# The line absent = on: the owner approved showing them with A9 and A10. =0 hides one again without a deploy (the API needs a restart to
# read these); a value that is neither 1/on/true/yes nor empty counts as off. The Admin Console's preview always shows them.
# FBI_CALENDAR_USERS=1    the calendar of a match: both teams' last and next matches and days of rest (F4, docs/owner/CALENDARIO_F4.md)
# FBI_KNOWLEDGE_USERS=1   the "Postpartido" block of a finished match: what happened, layer by layer (F7, docs/owner/POSTPARTIDO_F7.md)
# FBI_READING_USERS=1     the structured reading of a match: six sections of facts with their references, no AI (A9)
# FBI_NEWS_USERS=1        the news of a match and Home's «Noticias»: verified items with their source, status and link (A10,
#                         docs/owner/NOTICIAS_UX_A10.md); never an article's text
# FBI_EXPLAIN=1         «Explícame»: the frequent questions of a match, a pick and the parlay answered from what PrediGol already
#                         keeps - no AI (B9, docs/owner/EXPLICAME_UX_B9.md); 0 removes the buttons, the API answers 404 explain_off
# FBI_LIFECYCLE=1       each customer's state of the day (invited, activated, habitual, at risk, expiring, renewed, expired) with its
#                         reasons, computed by the messenger once a day (B11, docs/owner/CICLO_VIDA_UX_B11.md); 0 stops the
#                         calculation and keeps the history
# Switches of the worker (it needs a restart to read them). On by default; 0/off/false/no stops that work without a deploy and keeps
# whatever was already written:
# FBI_TEAM_CALENDAR=1     the feed that asks the provider for the list of matches of the teams about to play (F4; part of the day's requests)
# FBI_MATCH_KNOWLEDGE=1   the job that puts a finished match together in layers (F7; database only, no request to the provider)
# FBI_RESETTLE=1          the routine re-settlement of the picks of a match whose result was corrected

# ── The post-mortem and the memory (plan F8, docs/owner/POSTMORTEM_MEMORIA_F8.md) ────────────────────────
# There is ONE post-mortem of a selection (intel.postmortems, pm-v6). The two first ones - a match's (ai.postmortems) and a selection's
# (ai.pick_postmortems) - are frozen: their tables keep what they wrote and nothing reads them for what is new. FBI_AI_LEGACY_POSTMORTEMS=1
# makes the daily learning cycle write them again beside the new one. It exists to go back, not to be used; the worker needs a restart to
# read it. Off = anything but 1/on/true/yes.
# FBI_AI_LEGACY_POSTMORTEMS=0

# ── The weekly search for patterns (plan F12.6, docs/owner/PATRONES_F12.md) ──────────────────────────────
# Every Monday at 04:40 Bogotá, as the last step of intel_weekly, the settled decisions of the last 90 days are compared group against
# rest (market, line, model, competition, team, referee, coach...) on three measures, and what reaches |z| >= 3 is counted against what
# chance alone would give. It reads the database only: 0 provider requests, 0 AI, and nothing it finds reaches a model, a forecast or a pick.
#   off      the step does not run (the default, and what anything unknown means)
#   report   it runs and keeps a summary in the run's record (intel.runs, counts.patterns); nothing else is written
#   propose  ...and the findings that repeat in both halves of the window (at most 5) are proposed to the owner in Evolución, once each
# The worker needs a restart to read it. The whole reading, any time, on demand: python -m scripts.patterns search
# FBI_PATTERN_SEARCH=off

# ── The families in shadow (plans F10 and F11, docs/owner/FAMILIAS_F10.md and docs/owner/CICLO_FAMILIAS_F11.md) ──────────
# The goals of each half, the corners and the cards have models of their own (F10) and a cycle of their own (F11). Neither reaches a user,
# a pick or a model of the pipeline: what they write is research, under versions of their own. The worker needs a restart to read these.
# FBI_FAMILY_FORECASTS=1 writes their forecasts of the upcoming matches (family-v1) every FBI_FAMILY_FORECAST_MINUTES=180. On by default;
# 0/off/false/no stops it and keeps whatever was written.
# FBI_FAMILY_DECISIONS says what the worker does with those forecasts:
#   off      nothing: the families are not judged, settled or remembered (the default, and what anything unknown means)
#   shadow   one pass of decisions an hour (decision-fam-v1, never above Investigación, stake zero) and, at night, their settlement
#            (outcome-fam-v1), post-mortem (pm-fam-v1) and memory (memory-fam-v1); the post-mortem and the memory need migration 0118.
#            Seen only in Aprendizaje > Familias of the Admin Console. Back to off at any time: what was written stays.
# FBI_FAMILY_DECISIONS=off
